# Every live attribute in a crate marked verified that exempts code from a proof, checked by
# tools/check-external-body.py against the reason line beside each attribute. external_body exempts a
# function from the proof of what it does; exec_allows_no_decreases_clause exempts its loops and calls
# from the proof that they end. Fields, separated by tabs: path from the repository root, item,
# attribute, class, reason.
#
# glue      hardware or assembly leaf glue, the only unverified code CLAUDE.md allows
# gap       uses something this Verus cannot check: a raw pointer, a conjured permission, uninit memory
# unproven  plain code or a lemma with no proof yet, or a wait with no termination proof yet, so proof debt
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	flush_every_context	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest a flush, so only this makes the token
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	invalidate_iommu_all	external_body	glue	only the SMMU can attest an invalidate, so only this makes its token
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	load_translation_root	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest which root a core translates through, so only this makes the token
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	serial_write	external_body	glue	writes the PL011 through its memory-mapped registers, which have no state a proof could see
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	flush_every_context	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest a flush, so only this makes the token
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	invalidate_iommu_all	external_body	glue	only the IOMMU can attest an invalidate, so only this makes its token
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	load_translation_root	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest which root a core translates through, so only this makes the token
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	serial_write	external_body	glue	writes the serial port through port I/O, which has no state a proof could see
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_set	external_body	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_set_no_requires	external_body	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take	external_body	glue	clears a hardware page table word and returns it in one atomic exchange, since another core's walk may set the accessed or dirty bit between a read and a write
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take_status	external_body	glue	replaces a hardware page table word with the arch module's without_status of it in a compare-exchange, since another core's walk may set a status bit between a read and a write
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_perm_to_page_map	external_body	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	acquire	exec_allows_no_decreases_clause	unproven	the spin waits for the holder to hand over, and bounded overtaking is not yet proven
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	release	exec_allows_no_decreases_clause	unproven	the spin waits for the successor to link itself, and bounded overtaking is not yet proven
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	spin_hint	external_body	glue	the pause instruction, which has no state a proof could see
